    "conceptSummary": "Safely replacing a streaming Dataflow job with an incompatible version.",
    "correctRationale": "When the new code is incompatible, the update compatibility check fails, so the old job must be stopped. Draining stops pulling new data but finishes processing everything already read, so nothing is lost; unacknowledged messages stay in the subscription for the new job. Cancelling instead discards buffered in-flight data.",
