    "correctRationale": "A partitioned table lets BigQuery skip partitions outside the timestamp filter, and clustering on ID prunes blocks inside each partition. Queries keep the same table name and filters, so they need minimal changes. LIMIT and maximum_bytes_billed do not reduce the data read.",
