    "correctRationale": "BigQuery performs best with denormalized, nested and repeated structures that avoid joins. Appending new versions of records instead of updating them is cheap and keeps every historical state; filtering by the latest ingestion timestamp gives the current view. This keeps the model simple for both current and historical reporting.",
